      "writtenOn": "2020-04-07T07:19:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e we automatically start using the library as llndk\n\nThat is probably just because the dynamic linker tries to search the platform namespace prior to the vndk namespace.\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/linkerconfig/+/refs/heads/master/testdata/golden_output/stage2/ld.config.txt#329\n\n(note that \"system\" comes before \"vndk\")\n\nBut I think there is no benefit in allowing vendor to keep using it as a vndk lib even when the same lib is guaranteed to provide stable C APIs. Allowing it will cause another problem like double loading of the lib as well.",
      "parentUuid": "219c0a1e_a30fe0d4",
      "range": {
