      "writtenOn": "2020-04-08T00:10:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no. when a module is declared to have stub, it automatically goes through the ABI check.\n\n\u003e Orthogonality is king\nMaybe. But given that the most (in fact all) of the existing uses of stubs are to have stable C API, keeping this as an orthogonal issue and expecting module owners to know the storage/ram implication of the decision doesn\u0027t seem right.\n\nThis change was actually to address your comment in the bug \"can you also make this configuration an error?\", which I agree with.",
      "parentUuid": "6bec10a4_280f81f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 313,
